            <div class="step4-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Personality Traits</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/floral.png">
                <p><strong>The Lover Finds It Easy to Put People At Ease</strong></p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s rare to find an unpopular Lover; they excel socially and romantically which is mostly down to their uncanny ability to read people, to put others at ease, and their ability to understand what people need.They do so with such prowess and mastery that it&rsquo;s as if they have known their target for years, even if they had just met them five minutes ago.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Not all Lover Archetypes will have consciously made an effort become such prolific experts socially or romantically though; they are usually just naturals at it.</p>
                <p><strong>Socially Skilled</strong></p>
                <p>Lovers are skilled at relating to people because they can put themselves in the shoes of the person they are with and then understand or read their social queues exceptionally well.This skill means that they can then respond according to the perceived needs of the person.If you combine that talent with their ability to connect emotionally and then you can see why a Lover excels socially and romantically.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Unlimited In Love</strong></p>
                <p>Lover archetypes are boundless in their ability to express love to anybody and everybody around them. It doesn&rsquo;t matter whether the love they show is fleeting or intended to last in the moment.If a Lover Archetype sends out love at any time, they mean it.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>They thrive on giving and receiving love it's how they express themselves, and it&rsquo;s how they show others that they care.So, if you are around a Lover and they tell you that you mean a lot to them, even if they never see you again, it&rsquo;s important to realize that in that moment you meant the world to them.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Emotion Is the Lovers Nemesis</strong></p>
                <p>The Lover&rsquo;s ability to experience emotion is intense, but unfortunately, they rarely find others who can demonstrate the breadth of love to them that they crave and show to others.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>In some ways this is a similar challenge to that of the Caregiver Archetype, the difference being that the Caregiver gives an abundance of care and nurturing but rarely receives that level of attention back and for the Lover, it&rsquo;s the expression of love, commitment and intimacy they crave from others but rarely receive.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Unfortunately, the Lover archetype also has to contend with the crippling effects of unbridled, unfulfilled, unexpressed or excessive and overwhelming emotion as well as being in touch with and required to master all negative emotion too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This can pose a significant challenge to the Lover archetypes psyche and sense of self.So much so that many Lover archetypes grapple with the need for love and acceptance, being overwhelmed with emotion and having to balance their emotions to function normally in the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Lover archetypes, as a result of such challenges, often have a seemingly innate lack of self-esteem and usually spend their time seeking confirmation of their worth or emotional fulfillment externally (and even with the wrong people) which doesn&rsquo;t always solve the problem.Further, in this report, we take a look at why this might occur and how it can be resolved or reduced.</p>
                <p>If it seems as though the focus is too heavy on the emotional aspects of life for The Lover in this report that&rsquo;s because that&rsquo;s how The Lover Archetype rolls, it&rsquo;s all about the emotion to them.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It could be argued that the Lover does have too much focus on emotion and not enough on the practicality of things which is exactly what this report is reflecting. But there is no argument, Lovers do what Lovers do best, and that is to share emotion they just need to learn how to master it for optimal gain and an easier life!</p>
                <p><strong>Why Do We Hide Ourselves Even From Ourselves?</strong></p>
                <p>Every person has a hidden side. Jung calls it a shadow aspect, and it&rsquo;s discussed in great detail in our Premium Archetype Reports.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Here at Individuologist.com we realize that there is a hidden side or an unconscious world (to be more precise) that we experience internally, but we don&rsquo;t, or can't show or express this existence outwardly.It&rsquo;s this hidden aspect that can bring about great reward if we were to focus our attention on it. It&rsquo;s also crucial for helping each different archetype overcome their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Before we get started, it&rsquo;s important to acknowledge that there&rsquo;s also a hidden part of us that remains unconscious even to ourselves too and the process of individuation can help us to uncover these hidden aspects of our &lsquo;self&rsquo; too.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When we start to uncover these &lsquo;hidden&rsquo; aspects of our &lsquo;self,&rsquo; we begin to learn about what is really driving us.We discover the reasons why we do the things we do (or don&rsquo;t do the things that we want to do or should do).This gives us the opportunity to start to consciously reconcile these hidden aspects so that we can achieve our deepest desires or reach our fullest potential.</p>
                <p>In the case of The Lover, the stakes are high - they have big lessons to learn and the consequences of not facing their challenges result in profound emotional pain which is why we&rsquo;ve already started the discussions on the challenges that a Lover Archetype faces earlier on in this report.</p>
                <p>Even though The Lover is not afraid of emotion, there are still some hidden traits that they keep away from the rest of the world (or try to).The above is just a sample of some of these traits; it&rsquo;s not an exclusive list, but it&rsquo;s enough to give you a taster and to encourage you to get started on reconciling your shadow self.If you want to take things further, then you can find more resources and information in the Premium Archetype Reports.</p>
                <p><strong>Lovers Are Often Afraid of Being Alone or Lonely</strong></p>
                <p>People who have met a Lover but haven&rsquo;t had the pleasure of getting to know one might be surprised to learn that they are often afraid of being alone.It&rsquo;s something that most Lover Archetypes manage to hide very well because they are so good at reading and addressing the emotions of others and therefore distracting themselves and others from this fear.</p>
                <p>Perhaps this is the reason why they are so good at meeting other people's needs emotionally?As a way to fulfill their fear of being alone.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If the Lover could learn how to reconcile this problem, they&rsquo;d find that their relationships improved tenfold. Which means that it&rsquo;s probably impossible for a Lover to be alone in the future - because they are so attractive to others and won&rsquo;t scare them away with their constant need for commitment and reassurance.</p>
                <p><strong>Lack of Emotional Fulfillment</strong></p>
                <p>Lovers&rsquo; secretly desire somebody who can fill them up emotionally as well as the Lover manages to fill up other people. But unfortunately, they struggle to fulfill this desire because there&rsquo;s nobody who can do this quite as well as a Lover.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>When a Lover understands this, they truly step into their power.There&rsquo;s more about this further on in the report.</p>
                <p><strong>Gets Involved with People Who Are Way More Than They Can Handle</strong></p>
                <p>The Lovers fear of being alone or being rejected drives them to make commitments or take risks that can reach far beyond their means. And in some cases, this can potentially lead to the Lover being hurt, manipulated and controlled by someone else.</p>
                <p><strong>Esteem Is can be an Internal Issue for a Lover</strong></p>
                <p>Lover Archetypes tend to have problems with their self-esteem.More often than not they build their self-worth on the perspective of others, or the perceived actions or opinions of others.Lovers can be extremely sensitive to how others interact with them or make remarks about them.This sensitivity to the perception and communication of others has a significant impact on how a Lover Archetype views themselves and can be damaging to the Lovers confidence and esteem.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If a Lover were able to learn how to increase their self-esteem, without seeking fulfillment from others, they'd find that their life suddenly seems to be flowing in all of the right directions.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Learning how to work on improving esteem is a challenge for most people, but for the case of the Lover, the answers are staring them in the face.All they need to do is to recognize the message.&nbsp;</p>
